# EAS archive filter for LOCAL builds run with EAS_NO_VCS=1 + EAS_PROJECT_ROOT
# pointed at this workspace root (see app/package.json "eas:build:ios:local").
#
# Why this file exists: each workspace member (core/, mail/, calc/, …) is its
# own git repo and is gitignored at this root, and the root itself is not a git
# repo. EAS's default git-based archiver would therefore capture only the app/
# repo and miss the rest of the monorepo, so the in-sandbox install can't resolve
# @tinycld/core et al. Running with EAS_NO_VCS makes EAS copy from the filesystem
# instead — and when an .easignore is present it is used INSTEAD OF every
# .gitignore. So this file deliberately KEEPS the member dirs + coordination
# files (pnpm-workspace.yaml, pnpm-lock.yaml, tinycld.packages.ts, scripts/) that
# .gitignore would otherwise drop, while still excluding the heavy/transient
# cruft below. Mirror of .dockerignore (same "assembled workspace minus cruft"
# goal); keep the two in rough sync.

# Dependency trees — pnpm reinstalls them in the sandbox from the lockfile.
**/node_modules

# Per-member git repos (each sibling is its own clone). The build never reads
# git history and EAS_NO_VCS doesn't use git anyway.
**/.git
**/.gitignore

# Local PocketBase databases — never wanted in the build.
**/pb_data
**/pb_test_data

# Stray host-compiled binary left from local `go build`.
app/server/app

# Build/tooling caches and transient outputs (all regenerated).
**/dist
**/build
**/.expo
**/.vite
**/.vite-temp
**/tmp
**/*.tsbuildinfo
**/test-results
**/playwright-report
**/playwright/.cache
**/.worktrees

# Editor / OS cruft.
**/.DS_Store
**/.idea
**/.vscode
**/.claude
**/.superpowers

# Local secrets — must never enter the build archive.
**/.env
**/.env.local
**/.env.*.local
**/*.pem
